  "explanation": {
    "event_selection": "The unified specification uses only delivery-level search, approach, claim, pickup, drop, and publication events plus the color, claim-reception, pickup, and delivery observations needed to sequence one red, green, or blue delivery. Low-level movement and obstacle events are omitted because collision_avoidance already protects search_object, approach_object, search_zone, and approach_zone against obstacles.",
    "transition_design": "object_search repeatedly enables search_object and enters a color-specific claim-attempt state only after the matching object-visible observation. Each claim-attempt state abandons the attempt on the matching received_claim event. A successful claim immediately enables repeated approach_object; loss of visibility returns to color-specific object search, and pick_up_object is enabled only in the matching object-reached state. After pickup_confirmed, only the matching delivery-zone branch is followed, with repeated search_zone and approach_zone actions and visibility-loss recovery. drop_object is enabled only after the matching zone-reached observation. Failures return to retry phases, successful delivery is published with the matching color event, and delivery_done enables no further delivery action, enforcing one box per robot.",
    "feedback_response": "No previous-run feedback was supplied."
